{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CasimirZetaPrefactor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CasimirZetaPrefactor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.NumberTheory.LSeries.HurwitzZetaValues","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.casimir_prefactor_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.casimir_prefactor_pos","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirZetaPrefactor.lean#L76-L79","doc":"The prefactor is strictly positive (its sign as a *force* is fixed\nseparately by the `∂_d` of the energy; here we record the magnitude is\nnonzero, so the leading Casimir term does not vanish). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.casimir_prefactor_factorization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.casimir_prefactor_factorization","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirZetaPrefactor.lean#L68-L74","doc":"**Prefactor factorisation.** `(π²/6) · |ζ(−3)| = π²/720`: the\ntransverse geometric factor `π²/6` times the regularised cubic\nmode-sum `|ζ(−3)| = 1/120` is the textbook Casimir energy prefactor.\nThe right-hand side is `q`-free — no Hecke `y_λ` enters, because the\nleading-order modes are disjoint unknots. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.riemannZeta_neg_three_re","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.riemannZeta_neg_three_re","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirZetaPrefactor.lean#L62-L66","doc":"The real part of `ζ(−3)` is the rational `1/120` used downstream in\nthe (real-valued) energy prefactor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.riemannZeta_neg_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.riemannZeta_neg_three","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/CasimirZetaPrefactor.lean#L51-L60","doc":"**`ζ(−3) = 1/120`.** The Riemann zeta value at `−3`, from Mathlib's\nnegative-integer Bernoulli formula `riemannZeta (−k) = −B'_{k+1}/(k+1)`\nwith `B'_4 = −1/30`. This is the regularised value of the cubic mode\ntower `Σ_{n≥1} n³` that sets the Casimir prefactor. ","signatureChunk":0}]}